.TH COLORADO 1 "2026-11-08" "colorado 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
colorado \- one colour theme, applied to every toolkit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B colorado
.I command
[args]
.SH DESCRIPTION
colorado keeps a theme as a plain text file (semantic roles, 16 ANSI colours, fonts, cursor and icon theme, metrics)
and generates the exact files GTK2/3/4, Qt5/Qt6 (qt5ct, qt6ct, Kvantum), terminals, the holyc desktop, Firefox, fontconfig and xsettingsd read.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "set " NAME " [--only a,b|--all] [--reload] [--dry-run]"
The main command. Prints a diff of every file, backs each one up, writes it, and records NAME as the active theme.
.TP
.B current " [-v]"
Show the active theme and, per toolkit, whether its file is in sync, DRIFTED or MISSING. Exit status 1 on drift, 3 if nothing was set.
.TP
.BI "watch " NAME " [--reload] [--interval S]"
Re-apply (with backup) whenever the theme file changes.
.TP
.BR rollback " [list|DIR]"
Restore the newest backup not yet rolled back.
.TP
.BI "apply " NAME " [--apply]"
Like set, but a dry run unless --apply is given.
.TP
.B list, show NAME, new, edit NAME, export NAME GEN, check NAME, extract IMAGE, contrast A B, preview, generators
See
.B colorado help.
.TP
.B -tui [NAME]
Interactive editor with live swatches, a mock window, H/S/L sliders, hex entry, WCAG warnings; ? shows help.
.SH SAFETY
Nothing is written without a timestamped backup. colorado never calls gsettings or dconf and never restarts applications.
--reload only runs: tmux source-file, SIGHUP to xsettingsd, xrdb -merge.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
HOME, XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME choose where files are read and written. COLORADO_THEMES adds a theme directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
~/.config/colorado/themes/*.theme
user themes.
.TP
~/.config/colorado/active
the recorded active theme.
.TP
~/.local/share/colorado/backups/
backups made by set/apply.
.SH SEE ALSO
qt5ct(1), foot.ini(5), tmux(1), fonts-conf(5)
